        "answer": {
          "short": "2.46 marks",
          "worked": "Using $\\overline{x}=6.15$, the weighted sum of squared deviations is\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sum f_i(x_i-6.15)^2&=2(1-6.15)^2+(3-6.15)^2\\\\&\\quad +(4-6.15)^2+2(5-6.15)^2\\\\&\\quad +4(6-6.15)^2+6(7-6.15)^2\\\\&\\quad +2(9-6.15)^2+2(10-6.15)^2\\\\\\sum f_i(x_i-6.15)^2&=120.55.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sigma&=\\sqrt{\\frac{120.55}{20}}\\\\\\sigma&\\approx2.46\\text{ marks}\\end{align*}$$",
